		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: 1801 with OpenDM1801 running 12-22-2020 revision]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=1766&amp;p=15280#p15280"><![CDATA[
This is unfortunatly a known bug in the official firmware, which erases part of the CPU ROM memory used by the bootloader.<br><br>Its unclear under what conditions the official firmware does this, however once it happens, its not possible to update the fimware again, as the bootloader won't enter update mode.<br><br>The only solution to this is to connect a hardware programmer to the PCB and load a "modified" version of the bootloader which does not check the erased area of the CPU ROM<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Jul 20, 2021 2:04 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
