		<title type="html"><![CDATA[1801 with OpenDM1801 running 12-22-2020 revision]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=1766&amp;p=15269#p15269"><![CDATA[
I have two 1801 running OpenDM1801. 12-22-2020 revision.  I am able to read/write CP from/to both without issue.<br><br>The radios are working, but I went to update to latest Open revision on <span style="text-decoration:underline"><strong class="text-strong">one</strong></span> of them and it won't go into firmware update mode (no green tx led).  <br>The 2nd 1801 <strong class="text-strong"><span style="text-decoration:underline">will</span></strong> go into the mode just fine - but haven't been brave enough to go further until I resolve or just learn what is going on with the first radio.  They were bought at the same time and serial numbers are in-sequence.<br><br>I read that this may be a somewhat common problem and would like to know if there is an actual fix that doesn't require purchase of additional hardware to remedy.  After all, the radios were ultra cheap for what they do and they are working good enough.<br><br>Any comments would be appreciated.<br><br>BTW, to the individuals doing the coding on this project, ya'll are spectacular AND your work is very much appreciated!<br><br>Thank you. 7-3 N0GIK - Matt<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1896">n0gik</a> — Mon Jul 19, 2021 3:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
